I can't take this.

130
00:10:29,629 --> 00:10:31,564
Well, I can't take it back.

131
00:10:33,800 --> 00:10:35,098
Ooh.

132
00:10:39,305 --> 00:10:41,001
Does that mean you'll
have lunch with me?

133
00:10:41,474 --> 00:10:44,069
I'm sorry. I can't. I have
another business meeting.

134
00:10:44,244 --> 00:10:45,303
What do you do?

135
00:10:45,478 --> 00:10:47,913
Three other people and I are
trying to get a nightclub going.

136
00:10:48,081 --> 00:10:49,105
Country-western place.

137
00:10:49,282 --> 00:10:52,775
- Live music, dancing, beer, you know.
- Yeah.

138
00:10:52,952 --> 00:10:55,387
Thinking of calling it The
Country Club. What do you think?

139
00:10:55,555 --> 00:10:56,579
Can I see it?

140
00:11:05,732 --> 00:11:06,756
Hello, Jack.

141
00:11:07,767 --> 00:11:10,032
We got a meeting.
Thought we'd go together.

142
00:11:10,203 --> 00:11:12,001
Billy Wheeler, Jack Howard.

143
00:11:12,172 --> 00:11:14,573
Jack, good to meet you.

144
00:11:16,876 --> 00:11:19,641
- Come on. Let's go.
- We're just business partners, Jack.

145
00:11:19,812 --> 00:11:22,179
It's over between
us. I told you that.

146
00:11:22,916 --> 00:11:25,147
- Come on. Let's go.
- No, let go of me.

147
00:11:25,318 --> 00:11:27,219
Hey, Jack.

148
00:11:30,156 --> 00:11:32,455
You all right? I didn't
mean to hit you like that.

149
00:11:32,625 --> 00:11:34,958
I told you, Jack. Now
are you satisfied?

150
00:11:35,562 --> 00:11:37,190
I'm sorry.

151
00:11:37,664 --> 00:11:41,499
You'll be sorry.
You'll be sorry.

152
00:11:49,709 --> 00:11:52,474
- Count of three. One...
- How's this? This level?

153
00:11:52,645 --> 00:11:56,207
It's level. We gotta
straighten it out. Make it taut.

154
00:11:57,450 --> 00:11:58,890
- Like that?
- That's good.

155
00:11:59,052 --> 00:12:00,918
You can't do that.
We've got a deal.

156
00:12:01,087 --> 00:12:03,386
Well, look, you at least
have to give us a chance to...

157
00:12:03,556 --> 00:12:05,718
No, wait. Please. Let me...

158
00:12:09,662 --> 00:12:11,324
How could he do this to us?

159
00:12:12,131 --> 00:12:15,693
So this is it. I found these
lamps at an estate sale.

160
00:12:15,868 --> 00:12:18,702
This is the longest
bar in the southeast.

161
00:12:18,871 --> 00:12:21,397
The polished brass
is from Ireland.

162
00:12:21,574 --> 00:12:25,978
Hi, guys. I'd like you to meet
a friend of mine, Billy Wheeler.

163
00:12:26,145 --> 00:12:29,479
Billy, these are two of my
partners. Larry Boone. Kent Franklin.

164
00:12:29,649 --> 00:12:31,413
- Billy.
- Hello.

165
00:12:31,584 --> 00:12:32,950
What's wrong?

166
00:12:33,453 --> 00:12:35,333
If you'll excuse us for a minute.
- Sure.

167
00:12:35,488 --> 00:12:37,548
I just got off the
phone with Jack.

168
00:12:37,724 --> 00:12:40,990
Guess what. He's pulling out.

169
00:12:41,160 --> 00:12:43,129
- What do you mean?
- He's been to the bank.

170
00:12:43,296 --> 00:12:44,889
He has withdrawn his investment.

171
00:12:45,064 --> 00:12:48,694
Why would he do such a thing?
We're only a week away from opening.

172
00:12:49,135 --> 00:12:51,104
Oh, my God. It's my fault.

173
00:12:51,271 --> 00:12:52,705
It is?

174
00:12:52,872 --> 00:12:55,706
Well, I just dumped
him. He said I'd be sorry.

175
00:12:55,875 --> 00:12:58,003
I had no idea he'd
do anything like this.

176
00:12:58,177 --> 00:12:59,907
Here, call him. - What?

177
00:13:00,079 --> 00:13:01,824
Tell him you're sorry.
Tell him anything.

178
00:13:01,848 --> 00:13:05,410
Without Jack's money, we
can't open. And if we don't open,

179
00:13:05,585 --> 00:13:07,520
our money goes
right down the toilet.

180
00:13:11,691 --> 00:13:15,184
Excuse me. I overheard
your conversation,

181
00:13:15,361 --> 00:13:17,387
and if you need another partner,

182
00:13:17,563 --> 00:13:19,862
I wouldn't mind investing
in a place like this.

183
00:13:21,100 --> 00:13:24,764
- Oh, really?
- This may be a little over your head.

184
00:13:24,937 --> 00:13:26,577
We'll find another
way to raise the money.

185
00:13:27,206 --> 00:13:29,801
In time to pay everyone
and open the club?

186
00:13:29,976 --> 00:13:33,276
Yeah, that's a
problem. A big problem.

187
00:13:33,746 --> 00:13:35,339
Well, I might go in with you.

188
00:13:35,515 --> 00:13:37,848
We're talking
serious money here.

189
00:13:39,085 --> 00:13:42,112
Is 200,000 serious enough?

190
00:13:43,723 --> 00:13:46,283
You have $200,000?

191
00:13:46,459 --> 00:13:48,690
Yeah. I won the
lottery last month.

192
00:13:48,861 --> 00:13:50,625
You never told me that.

193
00:13:50,797 --> 00:13:52,493
Well, you never asked me.

194
00:13:53,733 --> 00:13:55,998
Billy, are you sure
you wanna do this?

195
00:13:56,736 --> 00:13:58,227
If I go in with you all,

196
00:13:58,404 --> 00:14:02,398
would you mind if once or twice
a week I sit in with the band?

197
00:14:03,743 --> 00:14:07,475
Well, Billy, for $200,000...

198
00:14:08,514 --> 00:14:10,983
- you own the band.
- Yeah!

199
00:14:12,352 --> 00:14:13,650
Yay, Billy.

200
00:14:28,334 --> 00:14:29,996
Get somebody on
this fold-up table.

201
00:14:30,169 --> 00:14:34,300
- Are they all full on the truck?
- Yeah, so leave this for last.

202
00:14:40,947 --> 00:14:44,213
Take the carpet facedown.

203
00:14:47,820 --> 00:14:50,051
You want the chairs first?

204
00:14:50,223 --> 00:14:52,715
Yeah, chairs then tables.

205
00:14:56,195 --> 00:14:57,993
What's going on?

206
00:14:58,498 --> 00:15:00,990
Our contractor got a
court order to shut us down.

207
00:15:01,167 --> 00:15:02,430
- What?
- He hasn't been paid.

208
00:15:02,602 --> 00:15:04,434
- Why not?
- Because Judy conned him,

209
00:15:04,604 --> 00:15:06,915
- just like she conned us. BILLY:
What are you talking about?

210
00:15:06,939 --> 00:15:08,908
She never paid him
or any of our suppliers.

211
00:15:09,075 --> 00:15:11,101
She just strung him
along and lied to him.

212
00:15:11,277 --> 00:15:12,973
Just like she lied to us.

213
00:15:13,146 --> 00:15:16,241
- Judy wouldn't do that.
- She would and she did, cowboy.

214
00:15:16,416 --> 00:15:20,478
All the money we gave
her? Gone. And so is she.

215
00:15:20,653 --> 00:15:24,954
No, no. No, she's not gone.
There's been a mistake.

216
00:15:53,786 --> 00:15:54,810
Judy!

217
00:15:56,622 --> 00:15:58,090
Judy!

218
00:16:03,496 --> 00:16:05,089
Judy!

219
00:16:21,314 --> 00:16:22,942
Judy.

220
00:16:28,521 --> 00:16:29,545
Oh, no.

221
00:17:03,356 --> 00:17:06,019
Place your hands on the
steering wheel, please.

222
00:17:11,397 --> 00:17:15,095
Maybe you'd better step
outside. Nice and slow, please.

223
00:17:25,545 --> 00:17:28,709
<i>Send me a letter</i>

224
00:17:29,382 --> 00:17:31,874
<i>Send it by mail</i>

225
00:17:32,952 --> 00:17:39,951
<i>Send it in care of
The Birmingham jail</i>

226
00:17:49,735 --> 00:17:57,134
<i>Send it in care of
The Birmingham jail</i>

227
00:17:57,310 --> 00:18:00,474
Well, there you are.

228
00:18:00,646 --> 00:18:05,175
Oh, Lord. Mr. Matlock,
she lied to me.

229
00:18:05,351 --> 00:18:08,412
Well, I know.

230
00:18:09,789 --> 00:18:13,055
- But she seemed so sweet and...
- Sweet and honest?

231
00:18:13,225 --> 00:18:17,993
Yeah, well, that sweet-and-honest
had a rap sheet as long as your arm.

232
00:18:18,197 --> 00:18:22,726
Her specialty was romancing young
fellas like you out of their money.

233
00:18:22,902 --> 00:18:25,531
But when I met her, she
didn't know I had money.

234
00:18:25,705 --> 00:18:27,799
The lottery, Billy. The lottery.

235
00:18:32,545 --> 00:18:33,569
Excuse us.

236
00:18:38,918 --> 00:18:41,581
Your name was in the
papers. Your picture too.

237
00:18:43,122 --> 00:18:44,886
It just seems so
hard to believe.

238
00:18:46,726 --> 00:18:48,319
She was a con artist.

239
00:18:48,494 --> 00:18:51,464
And the prosecution is gonna
claim that when you found out,

240
00:18:51,631 --> 00:18:53,827
you got madder than
hell and shot her to death.

241
00:18:54,000 --> 00:18:56,731
I didn't shoot her. I've
never even owned a gun.

242
00:18:56,902 --> 00:18:59,269
- Your fingerprints were on that gun.
- Yeah, but...

243
00:18:59,438 --> 00:19:04,968
And on the walls of the hall,
on the floor, by the victim's body.

244
00:19:05,144 --> 00:19:10,310
And you were seen leaving the
scene of the crime in a powerful hurry.

245
00:19:10,483 --> 00:19:14,045
And Judy's blood was on your
clothes when they picked you up.

246
00:19:14,220 --> 00:19:16,519
I was coming to your house.

247
00:19:17,923 --> 00:19:20,324
A neighbor called the
cops. I wish you had.

248
00:19:21,527 --> 00:19:24,520
I wasn't thinking right after
seeing Judy dead like that.

249
00:19:24,697 --> 00:19:26,632
Yeah.

250
00:19:27,199 --> 00:19:29,327
I didn't kill her.

251
00:19:31,337 --> 00:19:33,431
- I know.
- I couldn't.

252
00:19:33,606 --> 00:19:34,665
I know.

253
00:19:36,275 --> 00:19:38,005
All you can do is pick and sing.

254
00:19:40,646 --> 00:19:42,137
You think I have a chance?

255
00:19:43,015 --> 00:19:44,950
Uh, well...

256
00:19:51,590 --> 00:19:52,888
You have a chance.

257
00:19:58,097 --> 00:19:59,622
Guard.

258
00:20:00,032 --> 00:20:02,695
I'll see you at
the bail hearing.

259
00:20:05,204 --> 00:20:06,604
Okay.

260
00:20:43,576 --> 00:20:46,102
Boy, she rented this house?

261
00:20:46,278 --> 00:20:47,974
Two months. Paid cash.

262
00:20:48,147 --> 00:20:49,740
She told me she owned it.

263
00:20:49,915 --> 00:20:51,349
Yeah, part of the con.

264
00:20:51,517 --> 00:20:54,248
And causing you to spill that
soda on her was part of the con too.

265
00:20:54,420 --> 00:20:57,356
Yeah. You got the key? - Yeah.

266
00:20:58,457 --> 00:21:00,217
Now, the door was
unlocked when you got here?

267
00:21:00,359 --> 00:21:01,827
It was open.

268
00:21:01,994 --> 00:21:04,520
Well, you have to tell
us everything you did.

269
00:21:06,065 --> 00:21:07,397
I don't wanna go in there.

270
00:21:09,168 --> 00:21:12,263
You have to. All right.

271
00:21:17,009 --> 00:21:18,978
There weren't any lights on.

272
00:21:19,145 --> 00:21:22,343
So I felt my way along the
wall until I found the switch.

273
00:21:22,515 --> 00:21:25,007
Yeah. Where was the gun?

274
00:21:25,184 --> 00:21:27,384
Well, it was beside Judy,
and I pushed it out of the way

275
00:21:27,553 --> 00:21:29,920
- when I knelt down by her.
- Oh.

276
00:21:35,127 --> 00:21:36,322
Well, the...

277
00:21:38,798 --> 00:21:39,822
Look at this.

278
00:21:41,333 --> 00:21:44,269
That probably belonged
to Jack, her ex-boyfriend.

279
00:21:46,005 --> 00:21:49,373
Why don't I go see Judy's partners
and I'll meet you at the gym in an hour.

280
00:21:49,542 --> 00:21:50,840
- Okay.
- See you later.

281
00:21:51,010 --> 00:21:52,876
Okay. Yeah.

282
00:21:54,313 --> 00:21:55,679
That's, uh...

283
00:21:56,782 --> 00:21:58,478
So that's hard to believe.

284
00:21:58,651 --> 00:22:00,916
Judy was making cash
withdrawals to herself,

285
00:22:01,086 --> 00:22:06,115
instead of writing checks to your
suppliers, and you had no idea.

286
00:22:06,292 --> 00:22:09,194
None. She kept the books.

287
00:22:09,361 --> 00:22:11,887
Whenever we looked at
them, they always looked fine.

288
00:22:12,064 --> 00:22:13,999
I know who did it.

289
00:22:14,500 --> 00:22:15,991
So you didn't know
anything was wrong

290
00:22:16,168 --> 00:22:17,966
until you came
here opening night

291
00:22:18,137 --> 00:22:20,538
and found the sheriff
taking the place apart.

292
00:22:20,706 --> 00:22:23,505
- Not a clue.
- Well, somebody did.

293
00:22:23,676 --> 00:22:25,668
Somebody knew something
was wrong and killed Judy

294
00:22:25,845 --> 00:22:30,374
- before they came here that night.
- Yeah. I know who that was.

295
00:22:41,493 --> 00:22:44,759
- Hi, Leanne. I saw your car out fr...
- Hey, I want my money.

296
00:22:44,930 --> 00:22:46,922
- I don't have your money.
- Come on!

297
00:22:47,099 --> 00:22:49,059
The money you stole from
Judy when you killed her.

298
00:22:49,201 --> 00:22:50,241
Cut it out. LEANNE: Hey.

299
00:22:50,402 --> 00:22:53,804
I don't give a damn about you killing
her, but I want my 150 grand back!

300
00:22:53,973 --> 00:22:57,307
- So, let's go! Come on!
- Hey, hey! Hey, buddy!

301
00:22:58,244 --> 00:23:01,737
- Hey!
- Ow! Okay, okay, okay!

302
00:23:02,381 --> 00:23:04,543
I didn't kill Judy, and I
don't have your money.

303
00:23:04,717 --> 00:23:08,119
Yeah, right. I'm gonna get
my money back, cowboy.

304
00:23:08,287 --> 00:23:09,687
Hey!

305
00:23:10,155 --> 00:23:12,021
One way or the other.

306
00:23:17,830 --> 00:23:20,959
- Thanks.
- You're more than welcome.

307
00:23:21,133 --> 00:23:23,796
- Let's go find Jack.
- All right.

308
00:23:24,270 --> 00:23:25,761
Whoo.

309
00:23:36,949 --> 00:23:40,909
<i>Riding down old Two Mile Hill</i>

310
00:23:41,754 --> 00:23:45,953
<i>Tennis shoes up
on the handle bars</i>

311
00:23:46,525 --> 00:23:49,962
<i>Paying no mind to passing cars</i>

312
00:23:50,129 --> 00:23:54,362
<i>No doubts, no fears</i>

313
00:23:54,533 --> 00:23:59,403
<i>Just like when you are here</i>

314
00:24:00,172 --> 00:24:02,698
You sound just like that guy.

315
00:24:02,875 --> 00:24:05,743
As a matter of fact,
you're a little better.

316
00:24:05,911 --> 00:24:08,904
Have you ever thought
of singing for a living?

317
00:24:09,081 --> 00:24:12,483
Oh, I don't know. I guess I'm
afraid if I tried and didn't make it,

318
00:24:12,651 --> 00:24:14,643
I wouldn't have anything
left to dream about.

319
00:24:16,188 --> 00:24:20,455
Oh, come on. If that hillbilly
can make it, you can too.

320
00:24:21,093 --> 00:24:22,618
There he is.

321
00:24:24,863 --> 00:24:26,525
Let's go.

322
00:24:32,538 --> 00:24:34,268
Hello, Jack.

323
00:24:35,607 --> 00:24:38,008
You're the guy that killed Judy.

324
00:24:38,177 --> 00:24:40,737
They think I killed Judy.

325
00:24:42,181 --> 00:24:44,480
I wanna apologize for
taking a swing at you that day.

326
00:24:44,650 --> 00:24:45,674
You do?

327
00:24:45,851 --> 00:24:48,719
Hell, if I hadn't got ticked
off with Judy that day,

328
00:24:48,887 --> 00:24:50,913
I'd have lost my shirt,
just like you guys.

329
00:24:51,090 --> 00:24:54,117
Hi, I'm Leanne Mclntyre.
I'm one of Billy's attorneys.

330
00:24:54,293 --> 00:24:56,558
- Ma'am.
- If you don't mind me asking,

331
00:24:56,729 --> 00:24:59,961
what do you do that you
would have $100,000 to invest?

332
00:25:00,132 --> 00:25:02,431
Work construction,
save my money.

333
00:25:02,601 --> 00:25:04,763
Never date women that
can't pay their own way.

334
00:25:04,937 --> 00:25:07,406
When was the last
time you saw Judy?

335
00:25:07,573 --> 00:25:09,633
Day Billy decked me.

336
00:25:09,808 --> 00:25:12,539
Now, don't take this the wrong
way, but she needs to know

337
00:25:12,711 --> 00:25:16,478
where you were from about 4 to
6 on the day Judy was murdered.

338
00:25:16,648 --> 00:25:17,809
I was at the movies.

339
00:25:17,983 --> 00:25:19,474
- By yourself?
- With a girl.

340
00:25:19,651 --> 00:25:21,847
- What was her name?
- Shirley Hutchinson.

341
00:25:22,021 --> 00:25:25,890
- She work for a living?
- She works at Rowdy's bar.

342
00:25:26,058 --> 00:25:28,994
- What movie did you see?
<i>- Last of the Mohicans.</i>

343
00:25:29,161 --> 00:25:31,323
- Well, it was nice to talk to you.
- Yes, ma'am.

344
00:25:31,497 --> 00:25:33,398
- See you around.
- Nice talking to you.

345
00:25:33,565 --> 00:25:36,160
- Should we go? Bye.
- All right.

346
00:25:51,617 --> 00:25:52,915
Thanks for the lift.

347
00:25:53,085 --> 00:25:55,748
- See you tomorrow.
- All right.

348
00:27:37,656 --> 00:27:40,854
Excuse me, ma'am. I have
some business with your boss.

349
00:27:48,534 --> 00:27:49,763
Mr. Boone?

350
00:27:49,935 --> 00:27:51,535
What do you want,
you son of a...?

351
00:27:51,603 --> 00:27:53,203
- Why'd you bust my guitar?
- Cut it out.

352
00:27:53,372 --> 00:27:55,172
You broke into my room
looking for that money.

353
00:27:55,307 --> 00:27:56,468
- No.
- You broke in the room

354
00:27:56,642 --> 00:27:58,167
and smashed my guitar.

355
00:27:58,343 --> 00:28:00,812
You better get out of here,
cowboy. The police are coming.

356
00:28:00,979 --> 00:28:02,948
Let them come.

357
00:28:08,520 --> 00:28:14,824
Billy, I just hate bailing clients
out of jail in the middle of the night.

358
00:28:14,993 --> 00:28:17,233
Why'd they arrest me? Why
didn't they arrest Larry Boone?

359
00:28:17,396 --> 00:28:18,921
Because he wasn't trespassing.

360
00:28:19,097 --> 00:28:22,192
He was in his house and you
were beating the hell out of him.

361
00:28:22,367 --> 00:28:24,859
Well, he broke into my room.

362
00:28:25,437 --> 00:28:27,429
No, he didn't.

363
00:28:27,606 --> 00:28:29,370
How do you know?

364
00:28:30,509 --> 00:28:35,641
Because I had him followed
since he beat you up earlier today.

365
00:28:35,814 --> 00:28:38,079
He was in his office,
then he went home,

366
00:28:38,250 --> 00:28:40,810
and he was nowhere
near your room.

367
00:28:40,986 --> 00:28:44,218
Well, whoever did, broke my
guitar. Broke it all to pieces.

368
00:28:45,824 --> 00:28:47,952
Well, come on.

369
00:28:56,835 --> 00:28:58,098
Mr. Franklin.

370
00:29:00,606 --> 00:29:02,632
Mr. Franklin.

371
00:29:03,242 --> 00:29:04,266
Hi.

372
00:29:04,710 --> 00:29:06,576
You got a minute?

373
00:29:07,079 --> 00:29:08,240
Barely. What is it?

374
00:29:09,014 --> 00:29:12,951
Well, Billy Wheeler's
room was ransacked. Um...

375
00:29:13,218 --> 00:29:16,347
It was ransacked sometime
yesterday afternoon.

376
00:29:16,521 --> 00:29:18,717
I thought you might know
something about that.

377
00:29:18,890 --> 00:29:20,358
Now, why would you think that?

378
00:29:20,525 --> 00:29:22,685
Well, whoever did it was
probably looking for the money

379
00:29:22,828 --> 00:29:25,662
that Judy withdrew from the
bank before she was killed.

380
00:29:25,831 --> 00:29:27,299
That money belonged to you.

381
00:29:28,166 --> 00:29:30,795
- It also belonged to Larry Boone.
- Yes.

382
00:29:30,969 --> 00:29:33,302
But he doesn't have sap
from that big old oak tree

383
00:29:33,472 --> 00:29:36,909
outside of Billy's boarding
house all over the hood of his car.

384
00:29:37,676 --> 00:29:40,202
You'll have to excuse
me. I have a meeting.

385
00:29:40,379 --> 00:29:42,678
You know, I wouldn't
worry about it if I were you.

386
00:29:42,848 --> 00:29:45,181
I mean, if you did
break into Billy's room,

387
00:29:45,350 --> 00:29:48,230
and you were looking for that money,
that means you don't have the money,

388
00:29:48,387 --> 00:29:51,152
and if you don't have the money,
that means you didn't kill Judy.

389
00:29:52,758 --> 00:29:55,455
Well, I wouldn't know
anything about that.

390
00:29:57,029 --> 00:29:59,430
Besides, there are oak
trees all over this city.

391
00:30:00,499 --> 00:30:04,630
Oh, by the way, I heard
Billy's guitar was all busted up.

392
00:30:05,837 --> 00:30:08,170
Tell him no harm was meant.

393
00:30:16,048 --> 00:30:17,846
Shirley Hutchinson.

394
00:30:26,458 --> 00:30:27,949
- Hi.
- Hi.

395
00:30:28,126 --> 00:30:29,185
Can I sit here?

396
00:30:29,361 --> 00:30:31,330
Well, there's a clean
one right over there.

397
00:30:31,496 --> 00:30:32,930
Well, I kind of like this one.

398
00:30:33,098 --> 00:30:35,533
Suit yourself, then.
What can I get you?

399
00:30:35,701 --> 00:30:38,933
- Oh, club soda would be fine.
- All right.

400
00:30:39,104 --> 00:30:41,064
You know, the real reason
I wanted to sit here was

401
00:30:41,206 --> 00:30:44,734
so you'd be my waitress.
I think you're real pretty.

402
00:30:44,910 --> 00:30:48,005
My name's Shirley. Whenever
you need anything, you just holler.

403
00:30:49,147 --> 00:30:51,878
I'm Billy. How about
going to a movie with me?

404
00:30:52,584 --> 00:30:53,847
Excuse me?

405
00:30:54,019 --> 00:30:56,955
<i>Last of the Mohicans.</i>
Supposed to be a good one.

406
00:30:57,122 --> 00:30:58,750
I don't think so.

407
00:30:58,924 --> 00:31:00,790
- You've already seen it?
- No.

408
00:31:01,226 --> 00:31:03,855
You mind taking
your hand off my arm?

409
00:31:11,036 --> 00:31:13,062
Yeah. Yeah.

410
00:31:16,007 --> 00:31:17,999
- Jack Howard lied.
- Oh.

411
00:31:18,176 --> 00:31:21,510
Yeah. He said he took this waitress
to see <i>The Last of the Mohicans,</i>

412
00:31:21,680 --> 00:31:24,081
and I just talked to her and
she said she hadn't seen it.

413
00:31:24,249 --> 00:31:26,946
So he lied. He must be
the one who killed Judy.

414
00:31:27,119 --> 00:31:32,990
Yeah. Yeah, you know, it
always kind of bothered me

415
00:31:33,225 --> 00:31:35,660
that you didn't put
your money into the club

416
00:31:35,827 --> 00:31:37,693
till he took his money out.

417
00:31:37,863 --> 00:31:39,583
You think he and Judy
were working together?

418
00:31:39,731 --> 00:31:41,495
It's altogether possible.

419
00:31:41,666 --> 00:31:44,966
- I wish I'd have hit him harder, then.
- Yeah. Yeah.

420
00:31:45,570 --> 00:31:47,732
Let's see where we are.

421
00:31:47,906 --> 00:31:50,671
- We know you were conned.
- Yeah.

422
00:31:50,842 --> 00:31:54,836
We only think that Jack
may have been part of it.

423
00:31:55,013 --> 00:31:56,037
Yeah.

424
00:31:56,214 --> 00:32:01,983
And we have a pretty good
idea who busted up your guitar.

425
00:32:02,754 --> 00:32:04,154
- We do?
- Yeah.

426
00:32:04,322 --> 00:32:07,850
And we know what
to do about that.

427
00:32:08,693 --> 00:32:09,717
- You do?
- Yeah.

428
00:32:09,895 --> 00:32:10,919
Yeah.

429
00:32:14,499 --> 00:32:17,333
This is an old one of
mine, but a good one.

430
00:32:17,502 --> 00:32:19,232
I had it restrung for you.

431
00:32:22,073 --> 00:32:24,474
- You mean...?
- Yeah.

432
00:32:24,743 --> 00:32:26,336
Play something.

433
00:32:32,350 --> 00:32:38,051
<i>I'm getting out of this
High-rise penthouse suite</i>

434
00:32:38,223 --> 00:32:41,990
<i>Where we pretend
Life's rosy and sweet</i>

435
00:32:43,128 --> 00:32:48,726
<i>I'm going back to the
folks That I used to know</i>

436
00:32:48,900 --> 00:32:52,735
<i>Where everyone Is
what they seem to be</i>

437
00:32:53,171 --> 00:32:58,735
<i>I'm going back To a
better class of losers</i>

438
00:32:58,910 --> 00:33:03,746
<i>This uptown living's
Really got me down</i>

439
00:33:03,915 --> 00:33:08,910
<i>I need friends who don't pay
their bills On home computers</i>

440
00:33:09,087 --> 00:33:14,025
<i>And they buy their coffee
beans Already ground</i>

441
00:33:14,826 --> 00:33:22,324
<i>And you think it's disgraceful
That they drink $3 wine</i>

442
00:33:22,501 --> 00:33:27,371
<i>But a better class
of loser Suits me fine</i>

443
00:33:27,539 --> 00:33:34,173
<i>Yes, a better class of
losers Just suits me fine</i>

444
00:33:42,554 --> 00:33:44,614
Wait, wait. He's leaving.

445
00:33:46,992 --> 00:33:49,291
That's all right.
We'll follow him.

446
00:34:29,167 --> 00:34:32,660
I know where we are.
That's Larry Boone's house.

447
00:34:36,675 --> 00:34:38,439
Who do you think that is?

448
00:34:38,610 --> 00:34:40,636
I don't know. I can't tell.

449
00:34:40,812 --> 00:34:42,280
I wonder what they're up to.

450
00:34:46,017 --> 00:34:48,543
No good, if you ask me.

451
00:35:00,031 --> 00:35:02,151
- All right, freeze!
- Hands above the head!

452
00:35:02,233 --> 00:35:03,826
Police.

453
00:35:09,074 --> 00:35:11,236
Put your hands
on top of your head.

454
00:35:34,733 --> 00:35:36,634
So, what did they say?

455
00:35:36,801 --> 00:35:38,167
They were Judy's partners.

456
00:35:38,336 --> 00:35:40,896
Their original mark was Larry
Boone. You were an afterthought.

457
00:35:41,072 --> 00:35:44,600
They broke into his place for the
same reason they broke into yours.

458
00:35:44,776 --> 00:35:49,510
They were looking for that $350,000
they were gonna split with Judy.

459
00:35:49,681 --> 00:35:51,206
So neither of them killed her.

460
00:35:51,383 --> 00:35:53,978
They were in the lounge of
the River View Inn, celebrating,

461
00:35:54,152 --> 00:35:55,313
when she was killed.

462
00:35:55,487 --> 00:36:00,824
The bartender remembers them
vividly. They tipped him a hundred bucks.

463
00:36:00,992 --> 00:36:03,257
If they don't have the money,

464
00:36:03,428 --> 00:36:05,090
and Larry Boone was
ready to punch me out

465
00:36:05,263 --> 00:36:07,789
because he doesn't
have the money,

466
00:36:08,033 --> 00:36:09,524
and I know I don't
have the money...

467
00:36:09,968 --> 00:36:13,735
Billy, somebody's got the money.

468
00:36:25,283 --> 00:36:26,979
Yeah. Yeah.

469
00:36:27,152 --> 00:36:29,087
Here's the gun.

470
00:36:29,688 --> 00:36:32,556
Pictures of scene of the crime.

471
00:36:32,724 --> 00:36:35,057
- Stuff that was in her purse.
- Go through that.

472
00:36:35,226 --> 00:36:38,025
Yeah, see if there's anything
in there that looks odd to you.

473
00:36:38,196 --> 00:36:42,327
And this is the suitcase
she was gonna take with her.

474
00:36:42,500 --> 00:36:44,128
Okay.

475
00:36:45,670 --> 00:36:47,161
Yeah.

476
00:36:52,811 --> 00:36:54,211
What?

477
00:36:55,547 --> 00:36:57,573
It's just clothes.

478
00:37:05,223 --> 00:37:06,418
Well...

479
00:37:07,992 --> 00:37:09,984
Mr. Boone.

480
00:37:10,161 --> 00:37:13,290
Your Honor, Mr. Prosecutor,

481
00:37:13,465 --> 00:37:17,903
I wonder if I might have a
few moments of supposition.

482
00:37:18,069 --> 00:37:19,093
Objection.

483
00:37:19,270 --> 00:37:21,535
Your Honor, I have
to start somewhere.

484
00:37:21,706 --> 00:37:22,730
Objection.

485
00:37:22,907 --> 00:37:24,752
Your Honor, it'll just
be a few moments,

486
00:37:24,776 --> 00:37:27,610
and then I'll just
move right along.

487
00:37:27,779 --> 00:37:30,010
Mr. Matlock, proceed.

488
00:37:30,181 --> 00:37:34,710
But if I find down the road that
you've been messing with me...

489
00:37:34,886 --> 00:37:40,052
Your Honor, I've done a lot
of foolish things in my time,

490
00:37:40,225 --> 00:37:44,128
but I would never, I say
never, mess with you.

491
00:37:45,396 --> 00:37:46,420
Proceed.

492
00:37:49,667 --> 00:37:56,335
Mr. Boone, we... That
is, we, the defense.

493
00:37:56,508 --> 00:38:00,172
Started this investigation
with the belief

494
00:38:00,345 --> 00:38:04,578
that Judy Wilson might have
been killed by one of three men:

495
00:38:04,749 --> 00:38:08,413
Mr. Franklin,
Mr. Howard, or you.

496
00:38:08,586 --> 00:38:09,610
Not me.

497
00:38:09,788 --> 00:38:14,283
Well, the other two have
ironclad alibis. You do not.

498
00:38:15,059 --> 00:38:18,496
I was home all afternoon
that day, watching TV.

499
00:38:18,663 --> 00:38:20,143
- You can ask my housekeeper.
- I did.

500
00:38:20,298 --> 00:38:25,066
She said she heard the TV, but
she never saw you. So no alibi.

501
00:38:25,670 --> 00:38:27,571
- Well, I was there.
- Heh, heh.

502
00:38:28,473 --> 00:38:29,702
Well...

503
00:38:30,842 --> 00:38:34,540
this is a picture of Judy Wilson

504
00:38:34,712 --> 00:38:38,376
taken the night
before she was killed.

505
00:38:38,550 --> 00:38:40,416
- Did you know her?
- Of course.

506
00:38:40,885 --> 00:38:42,547
She was Kent Franklin's partner.

507
00:38:42,720 --> 00:38:50,253
Yeah. They took you for $150,000,
didn't they? How'd you feel about that?

508
00:38:50,428 --> 00:38:53,159
- Not too happy.
- Yeah. Heh, heh, heh.

509
00:38:53,698 --> 00:38:56,930
So, what first made
you suspicious?

510
00:38:57,101 --> 00:38:58,262
It was opening night.

511
00:38:59,070 --> 00:39:01,369
Sheriff's deputies came
in and closed us down.

512
00:39:01,539 --> 00:39:03,667
And you believed, at that time,

513
00:39:03,842 --> 00:39:06,277
that she had made off
with your money, didn't you?

514
00:39:06,444 --> 00:39:08,413
And my client's
and Mr. Franklin's?

515
00:39:08,580 --> 00:39:10,344
Yes. MATLOCK: Yeah.

516
00:39:10,515 --> 00:39:14,077
Mr. Boone, did you
know any of the workmen

517
00:39:14,252 --> 00:39:16,881
before they started on the club?

518
00:39:17,055 --> 00:39:18,079
No.

519
00:39:19,224 --> 00:39:25,789
How about Orville Hogan? Did
you know him? He's a carpenter.

520
00:39:26,364 --> 00:39:32,304
He says that he did some
work on your house earlier.

521
00:39:33,905 --> 00:39:35,396
Fortunately for us, he's here.

522
00:39:35,573 --> 00:39:37,303
Maybe you'll remember
him if he stands up.

523
00:39:37,475 --> 00:39:39,410
Mr. Hogan, could you stand?

524
00:39:41,813 --> 00:39:42,837
- Oh, yeah.
- Yeah.

525
00:39:43,014 --> 00:39:44,574
I remember. Of course.
I know Mr. Hogan.

526
00:39:44,716 --> 00:39:45,926
Yeah. Thank you, Mr. Hogan.

527
00:39:45,950 --> 00:39:48,317
It took some doing
to find Mr. Hogan.

528
00:39:48,486 --> 00:39:54,221
But he's prepared to testify
that he called you around 1:00

529
00:39:54,392 --> 00:39:57,089
the day Ms. Wilson was killed

530
00:39:57,262 --> 00:39:59,857
and told you that he
had never been paid

531
00:40:00,031 --> 00:40:03,559
and none of the other
workmen had ever been paid.

532
00:40:03,735 --> 00:40:06,000
Did Mr. Hogan call
you and tell you that?

533
00:40:06,170 --> 00:40:07,832
Yes.

534
00:40:08,339 --> 00:40:10,001
What difference does it make?

535
00:40:10,174 --> 00:40:12,370
I told you, I was home
all day watching TV.

536
00:40:12,543 --> 00:40:15,023
- Yeah, I know you said that.
- I was watching a football game.

537
00:40:15,179 --> 00:40:20,015
Yeah. And your housekeeper
heard the TV but she didn't see you.

538
00:40:20,685 --> 00:40:23,712
All she had to do was
come into the TV room.

539
00:40:23,888 --> 00:40:26,551
Sure. Sure.

540
00:40:26,724 --> 00:40:31,025
After Mr. Hogan called you,
you left your house, didn't you?

541
00:40:32,430 --> 00:40:33,489
No.

542
00:40:34,999 --> 00:40:36,467
Bailiff.

543
00:40:38,803 --> 00:40:40,135
Thank you.

544
00:40:40,772 --> 00:40:45,437
This suitcase belonged
to Judy Wilson.

545
00:40:45,610 --> 00:40:49,411
It was all packed and ready
to go when she was killed.

546
00:40:49,580 --> 00:40:50,660
Did you ever see it before?

547
00:40:52,350 --> 00:40:53,750
No.

548
00:40:54,385 --> 00:40:59,790
This suitcase
contained only clothes.

549
00:41:02,460 --> 00:41:05,658
Did you ever travel with
a woman, Mr. Boone?

550
00:41:06,264 --> 00:41:09,200
- Well, yeah. Now and then.
- Yeah? Heh, heh, heh.

551
00:41:09,367 --> 00:41:13,498
Then you know that,
usually, when women travel,

552
00:41:13,671 --> 00:41:16,368
they take more
than just clothes.

553
00:41:16,541 --> 00:41:24,244
They take hair curlers and cosmetics,
shoes and hairspray and earrings.

554
00:41:24,415 --> 00:41:26,884
This is only clothes.

555
00:41:27,051 --> 00:41:30,385
It only took me a
minute to figure out

556
00:41:30,555 --> 00:41:33,719
that she had packed
more than one suitcase.

557
00:41:36,060 --> 00:41:37,961
Where was her other suitcase?

558
00:41:38,663 --> 00:41:41,690
I searched all through her
house, her garage, her car.

559
00:41:41,866 --> 00:41:45,894
Not as much as a shoe bag.

560
00:41:46,537 --> 00:41:49,871
So where do you suppose
that other suitcase was?

561
00:41:51,809 --> 00:41:52,833
How should I know?

562
00:41:53,544 --> 00:41:55,376
The killer had it.

563
00:41:55,780 --> 00:41:59,774
Yeah. Because along with
the hair curlers, cosmetics,

564
00:41:59,951 --> 00:42:02,785
shoes and hairspray
and earrings...

565
00:42:04,122 --> 00:42:06,717
she packed the
money in that suitcase.

566
00:42:08,026 --> 00:42:13,624
And so, heh, heh, we went
to your house this morning,

567
00:42:13,798 --> 00:42:15,596
along with the police. Yeah.

568
00:42:15,767 --> 00:42:16,791
Guess what we found.

569
00:42:17,535 --> 00:42:19,401
- Nothing.
- Well, not quite.

570
00:42:19,570 --> 00:42:20,970
Not quite.

571
00:42:21,139 --> 00:42:25,975
We didn't find the suitcase
and we didn't find the money.

572
00:42:26,677 --> 00:42:27,975
But...

573
00:42:29,414 --> 00:42:33,351
we did find this watch.

574
00:42:33,518 --> 00:42:36,044
It's solid gold.

575
00:42:36,220 --> 00:42:42,820
And inscribed on the back is: "To
Judy Wilson from Billy Wheeler."

576
00:42:43,861 --> 00:42:47,491
The defendant, Billy Wheeler,
gave this to Judy Wilson.

577
00:42:49,333 --> 00:42:52,497
She was wearing it the
night before she was killed.

578
00:42:52,670 --> 00:42:56,766
Yet, this morning, it was
found in your bedroom.

579
00:42:56,941 --> 00:42:58,637
How do you suppose it got there?

580
00:43:00,912 --> 00:43:04,178
I'll tell you how I
think it got there.

581
00:43:05,049 --> 00:43:10,215
I think after Mr. Hogan called
you, you drove over to Judy's house,

582
00:43:10,388 --> 00:43:13,620
killed her, took the
suitcase with the money,

583
00:43:13,791 --> 00:43:16,590
then got rid of any
incriminating evidence,

584
00:43:16,761 --> 00:43:19,026
or hid it.

585
00:43:19,197 --> 00:43:22,599
Got rid of everything
except this watch.

586
00:43:22,767 --> 00:43:28,104
Now, why you kept
the watch, I don't know.

587
00:43:29,874 --> 00:43:32,537
But I'm kind of glad you did,

588
00:43:32,710 --> 00:43:38,149
because this watch is gonna
get Billy Wheeler back his money.

589
00:43:39,217 --> 00:43:41,311
And it's gonna
put you in prison.

590
00:43:48,493 --> 00:43:53,625
Your Honor, thank you for
those few moments of supposition.

591
00:43:59,437 --> 00:44:04,842
<i>Way down in Columbus, Georgia</i>

592
00:44:05,009 --> 00:44:08,377
<i>I wanna be back in Tennessee</i>

593
00:44:08,546 --> 00:44:13,985
<i>Way down at Columbus stockade</i>

594
00:44:14,152 --> 00:44:17,281
<i>Friends have turned
their backs On me</i>

595
00:44:18,756 --> 00:44:22,750
<i>Go and leave me if you wish to</i>

596
00:44:23,361 --> 00:44:26,525
<i>Never let me cross your mind</i>

597
00:44:26,697 --> 00:44:29,326
<i>In your heart, you love...</i>

598
00:44:29,500 --> 00:44:30,866
What do you think?

599
00:44:31,035 --> 00:44:33,027
Not bad. Not
bad at all, partner.

600
00:44:33,204 --> 00:44:36,299
Think he's as good at picking
and singing as pushing beer?

601
00:44:36,474 --> 00:44:38,773
- Better.
- You gonna keep him up there?

602
00:44:39,310 --> 00:44:42,178
- Yep. For as long as I can. Heh, heh.
- Heh, heh, heh.

603
00:44:42,346 --> 00:44:45,009
BILLY: <i>As I lay sleeping</i>

604
00:44:45,183 --> 00:44:49,018
<i>I dreamed I held you in my arms</i>

605
00:44:49,187 --> 00:44:53,921
<i>As I awoke, I was mistaken</i>

606
00:44:54,392 --> 00:44:58,796
<i>Because I was peeping
Through those bars</i>

607
00:44:59,864 --> 00:45:03,665
<i>Go and leave me if you wish to</i>

608
00:45:04,368 --> 00:45:07,497
<i>Never let me cross your mind</i>

609
00:45:07,672 --> 00:45:12,201
<i>In your heart, if
you love another</i>

610
00:45:12,376 --> 00:45:16,746
<i>Go and leave me,
little darling, I don't mind</i>

611
00:45:16,914 --> 00:45:21,943
<i>Go and leave me,
little darling, I don't mind</i>

